    "Using the <a href=\"#eq-SDI\" class=\"quarto-xref\">Equation 4</a>, we can detect seagrass patches that have darkened. Following the heatwave events, a total of 26.9 hectares of seagrass darkened, with the largest affected patch covering nearly 8 hectares. Overall, 24 % of the total seagrass meadow area showed signs of darkening between the 1st and 6th of September 2021. Comparing the spatial distribution of darkened patches with the site’s bathymetry reveals that 94.6 % of darkened areas are located at above 3.8 meters of bathymetry (<a href=\"#fig-Map_darkening_Bathy\" class=\"quarto-xref\">Figure 8</a>, A and B)."
   ],
